Confirmed live on origin/dev 64579cce2c. Compaction was left at the default 'Ask', and the chat sat at 86%, over the 80% trigger. Sending 'Reply with one word: done' was held before any provider call. The log shows console_context_policy_decision followed by controller_submit status=blocked, and the proxy saw no request. What the user saw:
- an empty Assistant row;
- a full-width panel reading 'Response accepted; waiting for dispatch.' with [Retry response] [Discard] (panel border 1.01:1);
- amber composer text 'Send blocked — resolve response recovery first';
- the header still saying 'Ready', and Inspect's 'What happens if I send now?' saying 'Run: Ready';
- the left-rail row showing ⛔ 'Blocked'.

The reason appears only after Retry. The turn then becomes 'Assistant Failed / Response failed.' with a System row, 'Conversation context reached its compaction threshold. Review and approve compaction before sending again.', which has no action. If the user picks Discard instead, the turn says 'Response discarded.' and the reason is never shown. Every later send in this chat gets the same dispatch panel.

There is no /compact command and no palette entry for compaction. The only 'Compact now' button sits at the bottom of header Settings ▸ Context and memory, about 20 wheel ticks down, and it runs without a preview. No Ask decision screen exists in the code.

One addition makes the finding stronger. Clicking the Model chip opens a popover that shows the numbers (Conversation ~165,672 / 191,904; Compaction at 153,523) and an Ask ▼ mode picker. It also names the lever 'Summarize older turns (/rewind ▸ Summarize)'. That /rewind 'Summarize up to here' path does have a preview (TASK-26017), but it is disabled in exactly this state: the tip is an unfinished assistant turn, whether retried or discarded. The disabled reason is cut off below the visible part of the rewind modal. So the one previewable way to approve is dead exactly when the hold happens.

fix_direction:
- Give a policy hold (ASK, or a real can't-fit) its own turn state, separate from dispatch-checkpoint recovery. Settle or clear the checkpoint so the generic 'waiting for dispatch' panel never shows for a deliberate hold, and never mark the turn 'Failed'.
- Show the hold in the turn slot on the first block. Use plain copy with the numbers (tokens used, budget and trigger), and offer one-step actions:
  - Summarize & send, using the existing TASK-26017 preview (what is summarized and kept, the token change, one extra call and its estimated cost);
  - Send without older turns;
  - Change the policy (Ask/Automatic/Off);
  - Cancel.
- Let the manual-summarize planner accept the held-tip state. Today /rewind Summarize is refused with 'Finish the current exchange', and that disabled reason is cut off below the visible part of the modal.
- Make the header, Inspect 'What happens if I send now?' and the Context chip say 'Next send will pause for compaction approval' once the chat is over the trigger.
- Add /compact and a palette entry, and give Compact now a preview.
- Add a 'When a chat hits its context limit' section to the Console guide and F1.

statement:
On origin/dev @ 64579cce2c the ✕ on a Console tab never closes any tab, and it gives no feedback. The finding's scenario (a background tab with a pending approval, a dialog, then Close) is just one case of that. I reproduced it on:
- a background tab with a pending approval (the finding's case);
- the same tab when active;
- a tab with a live streaming run;
- a tab with only an unsent draft;
- a saved idle tab that closes with no dialog;
- a brand-new empty tab.

In every case the tab, its run and its approval card stayed, with no toast, no reopened dialog and no log line.

The cause is not the confirm/re-check loop's silent returns. `_complete_close` (session.py:2796) calls `self._console_runtime()`, but `ConsoleSessionController` has no such attribute; its injected accessor is `self._console_runtime_accessor`. So every close raises AttributeError before anything is torn down. The worker started with `exit_on_error=False` (session.py:2852-2857) swallows the error, so nothing is logged or shown. This is a regression from b7dd8e53f2 (2026-09-08), not long-standing behaviour.

The dialog-copy half of the finding is accurate:
- The title "Close Console session?" never names the tab.
- "Closing removes this open tab" is ambiguous.
- All six count rows are always shown, including zeros.
- The pending tool approval is not listed.
- Stay has focus by default, which is the right safe default.

One detail is wrong: the '⌃2 Console !' nav badge did not light up after Close. It was already lit before the ✕ press, because of the pending approval.

Reproduced live on origin/dev @ 64579cce2c (235x52, ready mode, todo prompt, then 'Composer ▾' and the collapsed Stop). The bug is a race, not a deterministic repro. I ran 4 trials: 1 went fully stale, 1 went partly stale, and 2 converged cleanly within 3 s. An earlier attempt under the same key had 4 clean trials.

**Fully stale trial (t2).** Stop at 17:21:23; the backend logged 'run_reply end' at 17:21:24. At +3 s, +15 s and +72 s the card was gone, the header read Ready, the assistant read Stopped and the System message 'Response stopped by user.' was present. Yet:
- the three todo_create rows still read 'Awaiting approval', each with a clickable 'Review approval' link that only toasts 'No approval is pending.';
- Inspect read 'Run: Waiting for approval', 'Approvals: 1 pending · action required' and 'Live work: Waiting for your approval';
- the status strip read 'Approvals: 1 pending';
- the left rail read 'Agent: running · step 1'.

Alt+A toasted 'No approval is pending.' while those surfaces were still on screen. Nothing converged on its own for more than 2 minutes, and expanding the composer did not help. Opening and closing 'View full log' converged every surface at once (Stopped, Run: Ready, None pending, Agent: cancelled).

**Partly stale trial (t1).** The rows, Inspect and status strip converged by +3 s. The left rail kept showing 'Agent: running · step 1' for about 2.5 minutes, until the run log was opened.

**In every trial.** For about 1–3 s after Stop, the transcript already says Stopped and the header Ready, while the approval card is still mounted with live 'Approve all / Submit / Deny all' buttons.
